  <section id="purpose" class="doc-section">
    <h2>What the B-rep kernel is</h2>
    <p>The exact kernel in <code>packages/core/src/cad/brep</code> (24 source files, about 8 660 lines, plus tests) represents solids by their exact boundary: analytic and NURBS surfaces, trimmed by loops of exact edges. Everything is plain data and pure functions, so a B-rep serialises to JSON, crosses a worker boundary and diffs in the project history unchanged. Booleans, fillets and chamfers, hole recognition, mass properties, validation, watertight tessellation and STEP exchange all work on this one structure.</p>
