{"makeBox(60, 40, 15)    {\u0022V\u0022:8,\u0022E\u0022:12,\u0022F\u0022:6,\u0022S\u0022:1,\u0022surfaces\u0022:[\u0022plane\u0022]}\nmakeSphere(10)         {\u0022V\u0022:2,\u0022E\u0022:1,\u0022F\u0022:1,\u0022S\u0022:1,\u0022surfaces\u0022:[\u0022sphere\u0022]}\nmakeTorus(20, 5)       {\u0022V\u0022:1,\u0022E\u0022:2,\u0022F\u0022:1,\u0022S\u0022:1,\u0022surfaces\u0022:[\u0022torus\u0022]}\nmakeCone(10, 4, 20)    {\u0022V\u0022:2,\u0022E\u0022:3,\u0022F\u0022:3,\u0022S\u0022:1,\u0022surfaces\u0022:[\u0022cone\u0022,\u0022plane\u0022]}"}
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="geometry" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Curves and surfaces</h2>
    <p>Analytic types use the STEP (ISO 10303-42) parameterisations, so faces read from and written to STEP keep their parameters.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Parameterisation</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>line</td><td>C(t) = O + t·d, d unit, t arc length</td></tr>
        <tr><td>circle</td><td>C(t) = O + r(cos t·x + sin t·y)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ellipse</td><td>C(t) = O + a cos t·x + b sin t·y</td></tr>
        <tr><td>plane</td><td>S(u,v) = O + u·x + v·y</td></tr>
        <tr><td>cylinder</td><td>S(u,v) = O + r(cos u·x + sin u·y) + v·z</td></tr>
        <tr><td>cone</td><td>S(u,v) = O + (R + v tan α)(cos u·x + sin u·y) + v·z</td></tr>
        <tr><td>sphere</td><td>S(u,v) = O + r cos v(cos u·x + sin u·y) + r sin v·z</td></tr>
        <tr><td>torus</td><td>S(u,v) = O + (R + r cos v)(cos u·x + sin u·y) + r sin v·z</td></tr>
        <tr><td>revolution</td><td>S(u,v) = rotate(C(v), axis, u)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>extrusion</td><td>S(u,v) = C(u) + v·d</td></tr>
        <tr><td>nurbs</td><td>rational B-spline curve or surface (Piegl &amp; Tiller algorithms in nurbs.ts)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
